---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Serve the workspace to AI agents over MCP (stdio by default)

Usage: rustman mcp serve [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --http [<ADDR>]
          Serve Streamable HTTP at /mcp instead of stdio, on ADDR (default 127.0.0.1:8765)

      --allow-remote
          Allow --http on a non-loopback address

      --token-file <FILE>
          Read the HTTP bearer token from FILE (default: generate one and print it on stderr)

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
